      "id": "postgresql-diagnostic-guidance:1",
      "claim_scope": "The selected tutorial discusses index/filter predicates, matching sort order, LIMIT, bitmap scans, lossy rechecks, and example selectivity thresholds.\nThose thresholds derive from one reported table and cannot become universal planner rules.\nThe work_mem proposal raises per-session memory from 4MB to 30MB.\nIts 40 connections times six instances is a workload assumption, not a worst-case server-memory proof.\nGenerated-key columns and batch size are proposed JDBC deadlock mitigations, without a versioned reproduced driver case.\nThe source summary says immutable functions cannot use indexes, while another source proposes a wrapper for expression-index use.\nThe correct function properties and index expression remain unresolved; no unsupported SQL rule is adopted.",
